// A single token longer than the buffer a driver is likely to start with. A backend which collects the lexeme into a
// fixed buffer, or which grows one incorrectly, truncates the token or reports the wrong end offset. Nothing about the
// automaton is interesting here - the point is the size of the lexeme the driver has to carry around.
//
// The parser is not what this case is about, so the grammar is the single empty production the file format requires.

@scanner {
    WHITESPACE: /[ \t\n]+/ @skip;

    NAME: /[a-z]+/;
}

@parser {
    tokens
        : @empty
        ;
}
